          <Layout class="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.support.JScrollPaneSupportLayout"/>
          <SubComponents>
            <Component class="javax.swing.JTextArea" name="octofactsTA">
              <Properties>
                <Property name="background" type="java.awt.Color" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.ColorEditor">
                  <Color blue="cc" green="cc" red="cc" type="rgb"/>
                </Property>
                <Property name="columns" type="int" value="20"/>
                <Property name="font" type="java.awt.Font" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.FontEditor">
                  <Font name="Segoe UI" size="10" style="1"/>
                </Property>
                <Property name="rows" type="int" value="5"/>
                <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="(Cool Facts About Octopuses)&#xa;1) They have three hearts &#x2014; two pump blood to the&#xa; gills, and one pumps it to the rest of the body.&#xa;&#xa;2) Octopuses are escape artists &#x2014; they can squeeze &#xa;through any gap larger than their beak.&#xa;&#xa;3) They&#x2019;re incredibly smart &#x2014; capable of solving &#xa;puzzles, opening jars, and even using tools.&#xa;&#xa;4) Masters of disguise &#x2014; they can change colour,&#xa; texture, and shape in less than a second.&#xa;&#xa;5) Each arm has a &#x201c;mind of its own&#x201d; &#x2014; with two-&#xa;thirds of their neurons located in their arms.&#xa;&#xa;(How Sea Pollution Affects Octopuses)&#xa;1)  Plastic pollution harms their habitats, especially &#xa;the rocky crevices they hide in. Octopuses &#xa;sometimes use bottle caps or trash as &#x201c;shelter,&#x201d; &#xa;exposing them to chemicals and injury.&#xa;&#xa;2) Chemical pollution affects their brains, leading&#xa; to stress, confusion, and difficulty hunting or &#xa;avoiding predators.&#xa;&#xa;3)Microplastics get into their diet, since they eat &#xa;crabs and fish that have already swallowed plastic. &#xa;This can cause organ damage and reduce their &#xa;lifespan.&#xa;&#xa; 4) Climate change &amp; warming oceans, partly driven &#xa;  by pollution,disrupt breeding cycles and force &#xa;  octopuses into deeper,older waters where food&#xa;   is harder to find."/>
              </Properties>
            </Component>
          </SubComponents>
        </Container>
      </SubComponents>
    </Container>
